{"name":"Disco","hex":"#892d4f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"disco","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Clipping of discotheque (“nightclub for dancing”).","A genre of dance music that was popular in the 1970s, characterized by elements of soul music with a strong Latin-American beat and often accompanied by pulsating lights."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dance disco-style dances.","To go to discotheques."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/disco"}],"entries":[{"title":"Disco","blocks":[{"text":"Disco is a genre of dance music and a subculture that emerged in the late 1960s from the United States' urban nightlife scene. Its sound is typified by four-on-the-floor beats, syncopated basslines, string sections, brass and horns, electric pianos, synthesizers, and electric rhythm guitars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Disco_TGI_Bar_by_John_Vance.jpg/330px-Disco_TGI_Bar_by_John_Vance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disco","wikidata":"Q58339"},{"title":"Disco (Kylie Minogue album)","blocks":[{"text":"Disco is the fifteenth studio album by Australian singer Kylie Minogue. BMG and Minogue's company Darenote released it on 6 November 2020 in both digital and physical formats. After finishing her campaign with her previous album Golden (2018), Minogue was inspired by a Studio 54-esque section on her Golden Tour to create a disco-themed album. Early sessions began in 2019–2020, but were temporarily halted due to the COVID-19 pandemic and widespread lockdowns. As a result, Minogue continued to work on the album remotely from London, using GarageBand and Logic Pro for the first time."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Kylie_Minogue_-_Disco.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disco_(Kylie_Minogue_album)","wikidata":"Q97580032"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/db/Blue_disco_quad_roller_skates.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/db/Blue_disco_quad_roller_skates.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Blue disco quad roller skates","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_disco_quad_roller_skates.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Dance_floor_2_by_harmon.jpg/500px-Dance_floor_2_by_harmon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Dance_floor_2_by_harmon.jpg/500px-Dance_floor_2_by_harmon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Major disco clubs had lighted dance floors, with the lights flashing to complement the beat.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADance_floor_2_by_harmon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg/500px-ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg/1280px-ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg/500px-ZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The reflective light disco ball was a fixture on the ceilings of many discothèques.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZMF_2015_IMGP_0000.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG/500px-04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG/1280px-04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG/500px-04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Disco dancers typically wore loose slacks for men and flowing dresses for women, which enabled ease of movement on the dance floor.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A04232012dae_jpg_semana_de_la_cultura162.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Fotothek_df_n-15_0000413_Disko.jpg/500px-Fotothek_df_n-15_0000413_Disko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Fotothek_df_n-15_0000413_Disko.jpg/500px-Fotothek_df_n-15_0000413_Disko.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dancers at an East German discothèque in 1977. Due to the constant scarcity of consumer goods in the then socialist part of Germany, particularly more exotic fashion items like disco wear, people often sewed them themselves.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFotothek_df_n-15_0000413_Disko.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Vintage_DJ_Station_2019_by_Glenn_Francis.jpg/500px-Vintage_DJ_Station_2019_by_Glenn_Francis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Vintage_DJ_Station_2019_by_Glenn_Francis.jpg/1280px-Vintage_DJ_Station_2019_by_Glenn_Francis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu